course: dictionary
lesson: 2971
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The clues around a word tell you which meaning the writer wants. Drummer is one of these words. In «The band's drummer kept the beat for everyone», the clues are band and beat, so a drummer is the person who plays the drums.
explain: Sometimes the word is part of a phrase, and the meaning is not about drums at all. «March to the beat of a different drummer» means to do things your own way, not the way everyone else does. The word march and the idea of a beat are your clues.
explain: Older books and stories use drummer in other ways. A «drummer boy» was a boy who beat a drum to lead marching soldiers. When you meet an unfamiliar use, check the sentence first, then the dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: A drummer is a person who plays the drums, for example in a band, an orchestra or a marching band.
fact: A drummer keeps the beat, so that everyone in the band plays together.
fact: A «drummer boy» was a boy who beat a drum for marching soldiers.
fact: In old-fashioned US use, a drummer can mean a travelling salesman.
fact: In dragon boat racing, «the drummer at the front sets the beat» for the whole crew.
exercise: «The band's drummer kept the beat for everyone.» Who is the drummer? | A big, loud horn | A dance teacher who calls out the steps | A person who serves food in a café | *A person who plays the drums in the band
exercise: «March to the beat of a different drummer» means to do things what way? | Loudly, banging on a drum | Badly, and without any music | Very slowly, in a straight line | *Your own way, not the way everyone else does
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Many drummers and guitarists started on the recorder at school» that names a kind of musician. | started | *drummers | school | recorder
test: In «The drummer boy beat his drum as the soldiers marched past», what is a drummer boy? | A boy who plays football for the school team | *A boy who beat a drum for marching soldiers | A boy who drives the school bus | A boy who sold things from a cart
test: Why does a band need a drummer? | To hold the music sheets for the other players | *To keep the beat so that everyone plays together | To tell the audience when to clap | To sing the words of the songs
exam: Which sentence uses drummer to mean a person who plays the drums? | «Dad took the car to the garage for a service.» | «We ate pizza after the match.» | *«The band's drummer kept the beat for everyone.» | «The bird sang a sweet song in the tree.»
